triage:C5_QA2_REQ_C5_005 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C5-005" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_qa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f676f940af81b09315366feb4ca644b86a3d2485" ;
 triage:file "tests/integration/generation/test_observability.py:156; template/cargo-generate.toml:10; /tmp/c5-qa1-final4-validation.receipt.json; /tmp/c5-qa1-final4-validation.log:591" ;
 triage:issue "Actual exact-head f676f94 full validation completed with lint_exit0/test_exit5. Its single failure is test_sqlite_mcp_no_edits_sequence: Cargo.lock byte hashes differ after the lint recipe. All isolated default/Monty/custom-context/graph results and scoped build/default/Monty are successful, but the required full validation gate is genuinely failed, not merely pending CI. The generated-template lock exclusion repair already prepared by the C2/C3 owner has not been consumed here." ;
 triage:action "Consume the applicable narrow template Cargo.lock exclusion and its exact ignore-inventory/planted-lock regression repair from the owning C2/C3 checkpoint, preserving the no-edits byte assertion. Rerun the existing required full validation on the resulting source, retain source-bound isolated consumer/graph proof, and return directly to re-QA without waiting on remote CI. Do not weaken the no-edits check or fabricate a pass from focused receipts." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6649234798" .

triage:C5_QA2_ARCH_C5_006 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "ARCH-C5-006" ;
 triage:severity "BLOCKING" ;
 triage:reviewer "arch-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_qa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f676f940af81b09315366feb4ca644b86a3d2485" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron-commands/src/contract.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The promoted owner-schema repair preserves an input schema that the selected RMCP validator rejects. CronRequest::json_schema returns request_schema directly; that map contains only oneOf, with type:object present only inside each alternative, not at the root. RMCP3.8 schema_for_input requires the literal root type:object and rejects this shape. The explicit fix assignment required a canonical Schemars object root while preserving the typed Utoipa alternatives; naming Parameters<CronRequest> or asserting that oneOf exists does not prove actual input-schema construction." ;
 triage:action "Apply the native-map root type:object correction in the canonical Schemars JsonSchema implementation only (the C1 owner is preparing the compatible narrow correction). Preserve typed Utoipa oneOf and exact serialized DTOs. Exercise actual RMCP3.8 schema_for_input<CronRequest> or ordinary tool construction as a durable regression rather than only a type-bound or schema-text check." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6649234798" .

