triage:C5_QA2_FTQ_C5_001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C5-001" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_qa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f676f940af81b09315366feb4ca644b86a3d2485" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/tests/hook_environment/owned_child_unix.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The original indefinite wrapper wait is removed, but an inspector failure returns from stop before reaping the owned session leader. Drop retries stop and finally only sends start_kill, then drops the ChildWrapper. The owner can therefore return while its direct launcher is still alive/unreaped; the failure path has not retained ownership through physical completion." ;
 triage:action "Keep the cleanup error, but complete bounded direct-leader kill/reap before releasing its owner on inspector spawn, exit-status and timeout failures. Preserve whole-session descendant handling and the original cleanup budget; do not restore an unbounded wait. Add a causal failed-inspector test which observes physical reaping at the actual return boundary." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6649234798" .

triage:C5_QA2_FTQ_C5_005 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C5-005" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "implemented_pending_qa" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f676f940af81b09315366feb4ca644b86a3d2485" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/src/sqlite_cooperative_lifecycle_tests.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The regression computes G=now+25ms before spawning the ordinary stop thread. If thread startup or scheduling delays its request_stop past G, the old implementation publishes expiry synchronously in interrupt_if_expired and the test passes even though it installs no independent notifier. The test therefore does not deterministically distinguish the missing-notifier regression." ;
 triage:action "Add a causal witness that the non-entered-runtime stop installs/owns the future notifier while native work remains held, independently of the thread-start timing; then verify deadline publication before release/join. Use an explicit timer-arm/branch handshake or a controlled clock/wake seam. Increasing the25ms window is not a fix." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6649234798" .
